<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-to-build`>>

!! What to build (all in vessel-host.ts)
Today `surface` names ONE session and `surfacePost` posts to it alone; `moveSurface` picks a successor. Replace that model:
A. THE FACE CHECK. A session hears the vessel's surface only while (1) its `session.admission === "admitted"` and (2) its
`session.face === litVessel.face` (the face the lit vessel boots; `BrowserVesselResult.face`). Write one helper
`wearsLitFace(conn): boolean` holding both checks, with a comment: a session never sees a surface its face does not wear.
B. FACE-WIDE SURFACE TRAFFIC: `onRest`, `onPhase`, `onFrame`, `onControlResult`, `onCoherence` post to EVERY conn passing
the face check (`surfaceFanout(msg)`); a transfer list, where given, goes to none (these messages carry none; drop the
transfer parameter from the fan-out). `litVessel` is set after `openVessel` resolves, so a callback fired during the open
reaches only the lighting session's conn (keep a `lighting: Conn | null` for that window, cleared once litVessel stands).
C. PORT TRAFFIC RIDES ITS BINDING: keep `bindings: Map<string, string>` (binding -> sessionId). In `case "port:place"`:
* a binding owned by ANOTHER session refuses before the vessel: post
`{ t: "port:refused", binding, reason: "binding-not-owned", opening: m?.type === "port:open", ...(portId) }` (same shape
as the existing refusal) and never call `v.ports.place`;
* otherwise, after `vessel()` resolves and `v.ports.place(...)` returns `ok`, record `bindings.set(binding, sessionId)` the
first time (record the owner before calling place so a reply that arrives synchronously finds it; on a non-ok place,
delete a binding this call just recorded).
* `onPortMessage(binding, islandKey, msg)` posts `{ t: "port-msg", ... }` to the binding's owner conn alone, and only while
that conn passes the face check; a binding with no owner goes nowhere.
* `case "port:close"`: only the owner's close reaches `v.ports.close`; then delete the binding. Another session's close
of it does nothing (quietly).
D. A SESSION'S LOSS: in the house's `onDrop` (and wherever a conn's session ends), close at the vessel every binding that
session owns (`litVessel?.ports.close(binding)`, guarded: a vessel without ports or a throw warns and continues) and
delete them from `bindings`; leave every other session's binding alone. The dropped conn's `session` already nulls, so it
fails the face check and hears no more traffic.
E. Burn `surface`, `surfacePost`, `moveSurface` and every use (light() sets no surface; admitSession no longer calls
moveSurface; onDrop no longer moves one). The holder spawn's post (`standHolderSpawn((msg) => surfacePost(msg))`) goes
to the lighting session's conn (`conn.post`) — the holder spawn burns next step anyway.
F. True the header comment (lines ~19-20): surface traffic (frames, phases, rest, coherence, control results) reaches every
admitted session wearing the lit vessel's face, each over its own port; port traffic rides its binding to the session
that opened it alone, and another session's place on it refuses `binding-not-owned`; a session's loss closes its own
bindings and nothing of a sibling's. Name the owed beside it in one line: the vessel's active surface (`set-surface`)
stays vessel-wide, one per vessel, not per session (owed).

